  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A particle X has a small positive charge and is free to move. Y has a large positive charge and is fixed. X is initially moving towards Y.<br/><br/></p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>Y exerts an electric force F on X. Gravitational forces are negligible.</p>\n<p>The magnitude of the force exerted by X on Y is<br/><br/></p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">zero.</li><li data-label=\"B\">less than the magnitude of F.</li><li data-label=\"C\">equal to the magnitude of F.</li><li data-label=\"D\">greater than the magnitude of F.</li></ol>"
  },
